2. How do you manage secrets in Terraform without hardcoding them?

Use Terraform variables with environment variables:

export TF_VAR_db_password="mypassword"

Use Terraform Cloud/Workspace variables.

Use secret managers:

AWS Secrets Manager (data "aws_secretsmanager_secret_version")

HashiCorp Vault provider

GCP Secret Manager provider

Never commit secrets in .tf or .tfstate.

---

3. Difference between count and for_each (with use case)

count → Creates multiple instances based on a number.

resource "aws_instance" "web" {
  count = 3
  ami   = "ami-123"
  instance_type = "t2.micro"
}

for_each → Creates resources from a map/set, giving explicit control over each.

resource "aws_instance" "web" {
  for_each = { a="t2.micro", b="t2.small" }
  ami   = "ami-123"
  instance_type = each.value
}

👉 Use count when scaling identical things, for_each when unique identifiers are needed.

